{"id": "EUVD-2026-48834", "enisaUuid": "7a81eb82-ba98-3d33-a76f-e10c59b1b669", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: virtio: Validate control metadata from the device\n\nvirtio-snd control handling trusts the device-provided control type and\nvalue count returned by the device.\n\nThat metadata is then used directly to index g_v2a_type_map[] in\nvirtsnd_kctl_info(), and to size loops and memcpy() operations in\nvirtsnd_kctl_get() and virtsnd_kctl_put() against fixed-size\nvirtio_snd_ctl_value and snd_ctl_elem_value arrays.\n\nA buggy or malicious device can therefore trigger out-of-bounds access by\nadvertising an invalid control type or an oversized value count.\n\nValidate control type and count once in virtsnd_kctl_parse_cfg(), before\nquerying enumerated items or exposing the control to ALSA.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:51:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:48:37", "baseScore": 8.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3243563f99ef5d3949b934bd6390a5679405d0e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5da9742de22db0dbaa8d414214ab5e1bedde00f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21584672fd699abe1768241d6c501b2de6139b6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c77a6cbb36ff8cbc1f084d94f8dcda5250935271"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-64490", "GHSA-4qj6-j88p-jqg9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a78fcfb-6742-326a-a171-45023b1d1434", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.39"}, {"id": "50de8dcd-be09-3862-a99e-86b1fba581aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "53c58cf7-5f4f-3793-a887-3c0733e815b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6568e3de42dd971a1356f7ba581e6600d53f0a0 <c77a6cbb36ff8cbc1f084d94f8dcda5250935271"}, {"id": "5b74f1d0-d428-3d36-b35c-5626fb464e34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.96"}, {"id": "70061ff6-7e92-3623-bb78-74899cedc416", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6568e3de42dd971a1356f7ba581e6600d53f0a0 <5da9742de22db0dbaa8d414214ab5e1bedde00f9"}, {"id": "93f1206f-bc5f-3f2f-84c3-c98fdae61324", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.4"}, {"id": "9af3bb7c-0507-3f10-aa49-19804c460723", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6568e3de42dd971a1356f7ba581e6600d53f0a0 <3243563f99ef5d3949b934bd6390a5679405d0e1"}, {"id": "a2c86cc9-2738-38a5-a8a0-d32bfa926d74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ce922768-9e4e-3ba5-b24e-eab944b34558", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "fcce7639-1bdf-3127-bdf8-c2cf2590f994", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d6568e3de42dd971a1356f7ba581e6600d53f0a0 <21584672fd699abe1768241d6c501b2de6139b6a"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "94950250-8795-3bbe-8b01-b6b54ac3427a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}